<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
    Korea-specific naphtha (refined liquids) storage fraction for chemical feedstocks.

    Adjusts the non-energy-use remove-fraction from the GCAM global default of 0.75
    to 0.90 for South Korea, based on:
      - IPCC 2006 Guidelines, Vol. 2, Ch. 1: default fraction of carbon stored
        for naphtha/LPG/ethane feedstock = 0.80
      - Park & Patel (2018): Korea-specific naphtha storage fraction ~0.90
        (due to large petrochemical production and net chemical exports)

    Reference: Park, H.-C. & Patel, M.K. (2018). Naphtha storage fraction and
    greenhouse gas emissions in the Korean petrochemical industry.
    Energy & Environment, 29(6). DOI: 10.1177/0958305X18762446
-->
